.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-MACHINE-TRANSFER-TO-TEAM" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-machine-transfer-to-team - Explicitly transfer your enrollment to team ownership


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team machine transfer-to-team <team> <machine-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Give ownership of a machine you enrolled to the team. This changes who owns and can
revoke the machine, so --confirm must repeat the exact machine ID.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact machine identifier acknowledging the ownership or revocation effect

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for transfer-to-team

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team machine transfer-to-team acme m_abc123 --confirm m_abc123 --generation 9
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-machine(1)\fP
